{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01168",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.3,
      "end_seconds": 8.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "Doctor, I've checked them in and done the preliminary measurements, I'll hand them over when you ask."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.31,
      "end_seconds": 14.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.72,
      "end_seconds": 22.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.33,
      "end_seconds": 29.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "well, it's sneezing fits i thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.68,
      "end_seconds": 33.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.47,
      "end_seconds": 38.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Probably three weeks. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.6,
      "end_seconds": 48.72,
      "duration_seconds": 9.12,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.42,
      "end_seconds": 69.21,
      "duration_seconds": 18.79,
      "text": "Mostly mild. I'd say every other day. It settles a little with antihistamines. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.4,
      "end_seconds": 73.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.48,
      "end_seconds": 81.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a runny nose as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.96,
      "end_seconds": 92.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.77,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 92.83,
      "end_seconds": 98.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.16,
      "end_seconds": 113.29,
      "duration_seconds": 13.13,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I was getting to that! And, And there's a blocked nose at night as well, you know, two months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 114.19,
      "end_seconds": 116.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.44,
      "end_seconds": 120.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.87,
      "end_seconds": 129.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Yes, I had a mole taken off my arm, a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.54,
      "end_seconds": 131.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.58,
      "end_seconds": 136.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.39,
      "end_seconds": 139.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.47,
      "end_seconds": 146.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.61,
      "end_seconds": 149.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.39,
      "end_seconds": 156.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Uh, I'm on Foracort inhaler, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.74,
      "end_seconds": 157.68,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "mm, okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.71,
      "end_seconds": 167.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "Hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema my neighbour said I should get it looked at"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.24,
      "end_seconds": 172.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "how long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.67,
      "end_seconds": 180.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "About a month now. Rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_6",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 180.79,
      "end_seconds": 188.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "She is supposed to take it at night, but I can't say she always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.4,
      "end_seconds": 194.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "I take metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 195.45,
      "end_seconds": 200.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 100 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.16,
      "end_seconds": 205.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.46,
      "end_seconds": 211.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "not with me i'll bring it next time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.02,
      "end_seconds": 216.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.9,
      "end_seconds": 221.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "No, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_6",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 226.77,
      "end_seconds": 236.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "Erm, hold on, doctor, I think she reacted to naproxen once. I'm not certain, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.4,
      "end_seconds": 241.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Maybe, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.04,
      "end_seconds": 249.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.67,
      "end_seconds": 256.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Asthma, for five years. I have eczema. I have high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.37,
      "end_seconds": 261.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "so, anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.41,
      "end_seconds": 266.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.21,
      "end_seconds": 268.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "mm, okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.24,
      "end_seconds": 281.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.39,
      "end_seconds": 289.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "my father had bowel cancer. Okay, so my aunt has rheumatoid arthritis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.34,
      "end_seconds": 309.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "So, any facial pain, wheezing or rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.21,
      "end_seconds": 324.55,
      "duration_seconds": 13.34,
      "text": "No, no facial pain, no wheezing, no rash. I did have itchy watery eyes at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.02,
      "end_seconds": 329.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Did you get loss of smell or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.76,
      "end_seconds": 336.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "I haven't had loss of smell or fever, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.19,
      "end_seconds": 339.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.45,
      "end_seconds": 343.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.34,
      "end_seconds": 346.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.23,
      "end_seconds": 349.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 351.62,
      "end_seconds": 364.12,
      "duration_seconds": 12.5,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Temperature is 36.4 degrees, pulse is 73 beats a minute, respiratory rate 15. Oxygen saturation is 99 percent, blood pressure 109 over 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.84,
      "end_seconds": 366.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.71,
      "end_seconds": 372.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.54,
      "end_seconds": 375.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.97,
      "end_seconds": 388.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Chest is clear, no wheeze."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.35,
      "end_seconds": 391.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.36,
      "end_seconds": 404.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "The inside of your nose is pale and swollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.85,
      "end_seconds": 418.76,
      "duration_seconds": 11.91,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Okay, so my impression is this: I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at allergic rhinitis or a viral cold."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.08,
      "end_seconds": 423.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.06,
      "end_seconds": 436.98,
      "duration_seconds": 11.92,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like allergic rhinitis, but I'd like to confirm. I'd like to arrange an allergy test for allergic rhinitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 437.78,
      "end_seconds": 439.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Okay, I'll do it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 441.83,
      "end_seconds": 451.35,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "We'll begin with levocetirizine, 5 milligrams, at night, for two weeks. You take it by mouth. That should help with allergy symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 453.04,
      "end_seconds": 454.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 456.21,
      "end_seconds": 470.99,
      "duration_seconds": 14.78,
      "text": "We'll begin with fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, one spray each side daily, for four weeks. It's for allergic rhinitis. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 472.99,
      "end_seconds": 475.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Mm, you know, alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 476.09,
      "end_seconds": 501.03,
      "duration_seconds": 24.94,
      "text": "keep the windows closed in the early morning and wash the bedsheets weekly in hot water and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose book a review in four weeks let me check I've been clear what will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 502.21,
      "end_seconds": 517.59,
      "duration_seconds": 15.38,
      "text": "So, I take the levocetirizine, 5 milligrams, at night and take the fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, one spray each side daily. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 519.62,
      "end_seconds": 526.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 528.04,
      "end_seconds": 530.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 532.05,
      "end_seconds": 533.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "have a good day"
    }
  ]
}